# nr-tui-panels: integration fragment

Fills `mixdog_tui::panels`: the `/doctor`, `/usage`, `/context` and `/btw` controllers (`panels/{doctor,context_model,context,
context_refresh,usage,btw}.rs`). Nothing in it was compiled by its author (no cargo in the task); the lead compiles it with the
wave. The Node recording was produced and checked with `D:/mixdog-build/mig/ref/node` as the tree.

## native/core/Cargo.lock, Cargo.toml, mixdog-workspace-hack

No change. The crate uses only what `mixdog-tui` already depends on (`mixdog-js`, `mixdog-view-model`, `mixdog-tui-widgets`,
`serde_json`); no package or dependency edge is added.

## Protocol rows, SERVICE_PENDING, registrations

None. `/doctor` calls the existing `diagnostics/runDoctor` (registered by `DiagnosticsService`); nothing is added to or removed
from `SERVICE_PENDING`.

## What the wiring of the application task (`nr-tui-app-run`) applies

* `mixdog_tui::panels::PanelsHost` is implemented once by the application host (`type Picker` = its picker panel type,
  `surface()` = its `PanelSurface<Picker, ContextPanel, Value>`, `read_store(name, args)` = the store call that answers `None`
  when the method is absent, `clear_text_prompts` = `setProviderPrompt(null)` + `setSettingsPrompt(null)`, `close_usage_panel`,
  `notify`, `context_windows` from the state's `contextWindow` / `rawContextWindow`). Its method names differ from `SlashHost`'s
  (`store_has`, `read_store`, `notify`), so one type implements both.
* `SlashHost::open(Opener::Context, _)` -> `panels::context::open_context_panel(host)`; the run loop that serves the reads off the
  UI thread uses `begin_context_open` / `read_context_status` / `finish_context_open` and feeds the answer back (a claim lost in
  between paints nothing). `ContextPanel`'s `onRefresh` is the same `open_context_panel`; its `onInspect` is
  `panels::context::inspect_preview(host, &id, &revision)`, whose `InspectOutcome` goes to
  `ContextPanelState::finish_inspect(token, outcome)` of `mixdog-tui-widgets`.
* `SlashHost::open(Opener::Usage, Value::String(arg))` -> `panels::usage::open_usage_panel(host, arg)`. The run loop then, once
  per request (the `setTimeout(0)` of the Node code): `if request.due(host)` call the store's `getUsageDashboard(request.args() +
  onUpdate)`, give every streamed dashboard to `request.update(host, dashboard)` and the final answer or failure to
  `request.settle(host, result)`.
* `SlashHost::run_doctor` -> `panels::doctor::run_doctor(host)` (the core writes the report notice; an `Err` is shown by the
  slash dispatch as in Node).
* `SlashHost::btw_ask(question)` -> `BtwController::ask`, then (the microtask after it) `BtwController::dispatch`; when it says
  so, `store.askSide(question)` and its answer or failure to `BtwController::settle`; a dropped ask settles with `Ok(Value::Null)`.
  The session-change effect calls `BtwController::sync`, the unmount `BtwController::dispose`, Esc `BtwController::close`;
  `BtwController::panel()` is what `BtwPanel` draws and what `surface::layout` measures (`BtwPanel { done, text }`).
* The effect of `use-context-panel-refresh.mjs`: each render `ContextPanelRefresh::observe(context_panel_kind == "context",
  &ContextRefreshFields { .. })`; `true` means call `open_context_panel` again.

## Notes for the lead

* Tests: `cargo test --offline -p mixdog-tui` runs `tests/panels.rs` (golden `tests/goldens/panels.json`: 316 context models,
  5 context opens, 22 usage runs, 20 btw scripts). The recorder check is
  `node native/core/crates/mixdog-tui/tests/recorders/record-panels.mjs --tree C:/Project/mixdog --check native/core/crates/mixdog-tui/tests/goldens/panels.json`
  (passed against the reference copy of the same commit when the golden was written; sources are hashed with LF endings).
* `doctor.mjs` and `doctor-session-log.mjs` are not ported into the terminal UI: their checks, the session-log row, the report
  text and the `MIXDOG_DATA_DIR` data-folder hint are `mixdog-core-domains` `diagnostics.rs` (twin-tested in
  `diagnostics/tests.rs`); the Node `doctor.test.mjs` cases that remain the terminal UI's are the request and the error path
  (`doctor_asks_the_core_for_the_checks_and_the_report_notice`).
